he main  message here the main takeaway is that I  want you guys to sure you enjoy the  journey enjoy this time that we have the  Calm before the storm because I was  reflecting back today just honestly like  I said getting nostalgic thinking about  how far we've come thinking about the  Journey of Hogwarts Legacy to where  we're at now and here we are all the way  I mean early November almost to the to  Middle November it's going to be  Thanksgiving here in the US before you  know it and then the Christmas holidays  will be here and then New Year's and  then it's February guys and that's the  release date for Hogwarts Legacy we  could get you know early copies may go  out in January and while it's going to  be an awesome time and I know we've been  looking forward to this for so long now  just remember that once the game is out  and we're gonna love it and we're gonna  play it and we're gonna have an awesome  time or there's going to be a lot of  great videos made about it we'll never  be back here in this moment where we're  at right now and I say this to you all  as a long time fan of the Harry Potter  series some of my best times in Harry  Potter my Fondest Memories were the  anticipation it was the journey it was  the anticipation the books were great  finally getting to read what happens who  lives who dies Who falls in love and how  the story finally ends yes that was a  title of a muggle net book all that was  great and I and I loved the story but so  much about the journey was about the  before times it was about the in-between  it was about the conversations it was  about the podcast it was about the  fanfics it was about all these other  things that happened around it and  that's not to say that this stuff won't  keep happening after Hogwarts Legacy  comes out I'm certainly gonna keep  covering the game as long as you guys  are interested hopefully we'll get  sequels hopefully we'll get I don't know  multiplayer components maybe they'll  decide to do a mu